counterfactuals.output:
A vehicle test bench wheel mount comprising:

a floating plate configured to support at least one vehicle wheel during testing;

at least one roller disposed on the floating plate and configured to contact the vehicle wheel at a wheel contact point, the at least one roller being movable in a substantially horizontal plane;

a roller-supporting plate portion carrying the at least one roller and being rotatable relative to the floating plate; and

at least one actuator operatively coupled to the roller-supporting plate portion and configured to rotate the roller-supporting plate portion about a selectable substantially vertical axis;

wherein the selectable substantially vertical axis is positionable, with respect to a travel direction of the vehicle wheel, either forward of the wheel contact point or rearward of the wheel contact point, such that the orientation and lateral position of the at least one roller relative to the vehicle wheel are adjustable to simulate steering, slip, or alignment conditions on the vehicle test bench.
